# Linear tickets follow product flow

When creating or ordering Linear issues:

## Do

- Follow the product: mobile catalog and listening first, then Artist Studio web, then public pages.
- Keep a journey in one line: schema → seed → a tab or list the fan can open → the detail screen that list opens.
- Every phone slice must be reachable by tapping through the app when it is Done. No orphan screens.
- If the numbered list and that order disagree, the product order wins. Leave the later ticket in Todo.

## Phone catalog after the tab shell

1. Discover (KIND-53)
2. Artist profile and track detail (KIND-51)
3. Library (KIND-52)
4. Audio spike → player → mini-player craft (KIND-54 → KIND-55 → KIND-56)
5. Home feed (KIND-57)

Do not put KIND-51 before Discover.

## Do not

- Jump phone → web → phone to finish an epic
- Start KIND-45 (web Studio sign-in) before catalog, seed, and the mobile shell unless this message says to
- Build a detail screen with no tab or list that opens it

## Example

Bad: onboarding (phone) → Studio sign-in (web) → catalog tables (phone).

Bad: tab shell → artist profile (no door) → Discover.

Good: onboarding → catalog schema → seed → tab shell → Discover → artist and track. Circle back to Studio sign-in when the phone core is standing.
